{"id": "sdqa0121", "pool": "sdqa", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Exponent iation is a math ematic operation where you multi ply a number by itself repeatedly. For example if you have two to the power of three that means two times two times two which equal s eight. The small number on top is called the exponent and tells you how many times to multiply the base number by itself.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
